\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. To the hills I lift mine eyes,
\par The everlasting hills;
\par Streaming thence in fresh supplies,
\par My soul the Spirit feels.
\par Will He not His help afford?
\par Help, while yet I ask, is given:
\par God comes down: the God and Lord
\par That made both earth and heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Faithful soul, pray always; pray,
\par And still in God confide;
\par He thy feeble steps shall stay,
\par Nor suffer thee to slide:
\par Lean on thy Redeemer's breast;
\par He thy quiet spirit keeps;
\par Rest in Him, securely rest;
\par Thy watchman never sleeps.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Neither sin, nor earth, nor hell
\par Thy keeper can surprise;
\par Careless slumbers cannot steal
\par On His all- seeing eyes:
\par He is Israel's sure defence;
\par Israel all His care shall prove,
\par Kept by watchful providence
\par And ever- waking love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. See the Lord, thy keeper, stand
\par Omnipotently near!
\par Lo! He holds thee by thy hand,
\par And banishes thy fear;
\par Shadows with His wings thy head;
\par Guards from all impending harms:
\par Round thee and beneath are spread
\par The everlasting arms.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Christ shall bless thy going out,
\par Shall bless thy coming in;
\par Kindly compass thee about,
\par Till thou art saved from sin;
\par Like thy spotless Master, thou,
\par Filled with wisdom, 
\par love and power,
\par Henceforth, and evermore.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

